Here's the shape of a block decorator on this storefront.

## The basics

Every block is two files in `components/eds-storefront/blocks/<blockname>/`:
- `blockname.js` — exports one default async `decorate(block)` function
- `blockname.css` — styles, every selector scoped under `.blockname`

AEM turns the authored table into nested divs (each row → a `div`, each cell → a `div` inside it) and calls your `decorate` with the block element automatically.

## Decorator structure, in order

```javascript
export default async function decorate(block) {
  // 1. Guard against empty content
  if (!block.children.length) return;

  // 2. Extract config (if your first row is settings, read it then remove it)
  // 3. Read the rows — never assume a cell exists
  const rows = [...block.children];

  // 4. Rebuild the DOM
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  container.classList.add('blockname-items');
  rows.forEach((row) => {
    const title = row.children[0]?.textContent.trim();
    if (!title) return;                        // skip malformed rows
    const img = row.children[1]?.querySelector('picture'); // optional field
    // ...build the item, append to container
  });
  block.textContent = '';
  block.append(container);

  // 5. Wire events last (prefer delegation on the block itself)
  block.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = e.target.closest('button');
    if (btn) { /* handle */ }
  });
}
```

Check variants with `block.classList.contains('variant-name')` — variant names from the table header land as extra classes.

## Rules specific to this storefront

- **Typography:** in the CSS, use `font: var(--type-...)` from `styles/styles.css` for every text style. Don't write a `font-size`, and don't copy one from a boilerplate block.
- **Drop-ins:** if the block touches any Commerce drop-in (containers, slots, events, `@dropins/*/api.js`), that part must go through the drop-in developer skill — don't inline it. Keep the decorator to layout and plain DOM work.
- **Before writing anything:** look at what's already in the `blocks/` folder. Reuse or adapt an existing block if one is close; only build from scratch if nothing fits, and note why.
- **Inspect the real HTML first** — `curl <preview-url>/page.plain.html` or `console.log(block.outerHTML)` — instead of guessing the row/cell layout.

## The three mistakes that bite most

1. `row.children[1].textContent` with no `?.` — crashes when an author omits a field.
2. Clearing a cell's HTML before moving its image out — the image is destroyed. Move or clone first.
3. Unscoped CSS like `.item { ... }` — it leaks into every other block on the page.

When the block is done: `sync_storefront` pushes it live, and the register-custom-block skill makes it draggable in DA.live if authors need it. Happy to scaffold a real one — just tell me what the block should do.
